# Feature 12 — AI Copy Chat

## Goal
A dedicated conversational AI assistant at /chat that lets any 
Lahjah user get quick copy suggestions by describing their need 
or uploading a screenshot — without going through the full 
structured request workflow.

## Context
Designers often need quick copy variations for UI elements while 
working in Figma. Instead of switching to ChatGPT, they can use 
Lahjah's chat which understands HungerStation's brand voice and 
copy guidelines.

## Access
- Available to both Designers and Copy Team
- Requires authentication (auth-guarded like all other pages)
- Accessible via /chat route
- Add "Chat" link in the main navigation

## UI Layout
- Full page chat interface at /chat
- Left sidebar (if space allows): list of past conversations
  - Each conversation shows first message as title + date
  - "New chat" button at the top of sidebar
  - Click conversation to load it
- Main area: chat window
  - Messages displayed in bubbles (user right, AI left)
  - User bubbles: #222629 background, white text
  - AI bubbles: white background, #222629 text, subtle border
  - Timestamps on each message
  - If an image was uploaded, show thumbnail in the message bubble
- Bottom input area:
  - Text input field: "Ask Lahjah anything about copy..."
  - Image upload button (paperclip or image icon)
  - Language toggle: EN / AR (defaults to EN)
  - Send button (yellow #FFEA00, #222629 text)
  - Pressing Enter sends the message

## Image Upload
- User can attach one image per message (Figma screenshot etc.)
- Accepted formats: PNG, JPG, WEBP
- Image is sent to the AI as context alongside the text prompt
- Show image preview in the input area before sending
- Use existing Firebase Storage for image uploads
- Store image URL in the message document in Firestore

## AI Behavior
- Use the existing Anthropic API (same as copy generation)
- System prompt:
  "You are Lahjah, an AI copy assistant for HungerStation's 
  product and design teams. You help designers and writers 
  create clear, on-brand UI copy in English and Arabic. 
  You understand HungerStation's tone: friendly, clear, 
  and culturally relevant for MENA markets. When given a 
  screenshot, describe what UI elements you see and suggest 
  copy for them. Always provide suggestions in the language 
  the user requests (EN or AR). For Arabic, use Gulf dialect 
  that feels natural for a food delivery app."
- Send full conversation history with each request for context
- If image is attached, send as base64 in the API message
- Language toggle value is appended to each user message:
  "[Respond in English]" or "[Respond in Arabic]"

## Firestore Data Structure
Collection: chats/{userId}/conversations/{conversationId}
- conversationId (auto-generated)
- title (first user message, truncated to 50 chars)
- createdAt (timestamp)
- updatedAt (timestamp)

Sub-collection: chats/{userId}/conversations/{conversationId}/messages/{messageId}
- role ("user" | "assistant")
- content (text)
- imageUrl (optional, string)
- language ("en" | "ar")
- createdAt (timestamp)

